    "title": "Fast food chain continues Central Kentucky expansion with new restaurant opening - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brian Simms ,\n9 hours ago A Chicken Burrito Bowl from Chipotle Mexican Grill, which has more than 4,000 locations globally. Richmond is opening its first location July 16. Provided A new-to-Richmond fast food chain is opening in the Central Kentucky town.\nChipotle Mexican Grill is opening its first location in Richmond at 10:45 a.m. on Thursday, July 16. The new restaurant is located at 863 Eastern Bypass, near Hobby Lobby and Menards.\nThe fast-casual restaurant chain specializes in bowls, tacos and burritos made to order in front of the customer. The new location is part of a massive expansion of Chipotle restaurants in recent years in Central Kentucky . New locations have opened or opening soon in Lexington, Georgetown, Frankfort and Nicholasville.\nThe new Richmond location will feature a “Chipotlane,” a drive-thru pick-up lane that allows guests to pick up digital orders without leaving their cars. It will also have the restaurant’s new high protein menu with dishes that range from 15 to 81 grams of protein per item.\nRichmond’s new Chipotle restaurant is currently hiring.\nChipotle Mexican Grill, Richmond Where: 863 Eastern Bypass\nHours: 10:45 a.m - 10 p.m. daily\nOrder online: chipotle.com\nPsychedelic pizza chain plans to reopen in Lexington. Here’s when and where\nPopular closed Lexington restaurant is back with another pop up.\n3",
    "summary": "9 hours ago A Chicken Burrito Bowl from Chipotle Mexican Grill, which has more than 4,000 locations globally. The fast-casual restaurant chain specializes in bowls, tacos and burritos made to order in front of the customer. The new location is part of a massive expansion of Chipotle restaurants in recent years in Central Kentucky . The new Richmond location will feature a “Chipotlane,” a drive-thru pick-up lane that allows guests to pick up digital orders without leaving their cars.",
